                        "type": "rich_text_section",
                        "elements": [
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "If the Forum producers have reached out to you it's pretty clear they plan on doing the show. When I worked there as a fill-in we'd be careful not to promise that the show would happen or when. We'd also usually reach out to more people than we could use, so you may or may not be  in the final cut. It shows a real appreciation of your work that they reached out to you, so crossing fingers. If you're comfortable with the idea, make it clear you are OK with being in studio. That will improve the odds they use you and people actually sitting in the studio generally get asked more questions and get more air time."
                            }
